Changes from Ymir 1.0.4:
- core is a Kotlin Multiplatform library for Android, iosArm64 and iosSimulatorArm64, built on
  the JetBrains lifecycle and the Compose Multiplatform runtime. Its sources moved from
  core/src/main/java to core/src/commonMain/kotlin and keep the io.github.lucascordeiro.ymir.core
  package.
- LifecycleUtils takes LocalLifecycleOwner from androidx.lifecycle.compose instead of
  androidx.compose.ui.platform, so it compiles for iOS.
- Unused imports were removed from action/Action.kt, action/ViewModel.kt, state/ViewModel.kt and
  utils/LifecycleUtils.kt.
- core has common tests that run on the Android host and on the iOS simulator.
- The build uses Gradle 8.14.2, AGP 8.11.0, Kotlin 2.4.20 and JVM 17.
